{
 "about": "buildTiming input and output for TIMING_VERSION cuando-vender-2 (contract C8, revision 3). Input points may carry dt and sold (a sell-through sample of the interval (t - dt, t]; valid when dt is an integer 600..7200 and sold an integer 0..1000000). Every column of cuando-vender-1 is unchanged. Samples: (1) one per person and moment (same person and t: the larger dt, equal dt: the larger sold); (2) per item, sorted by dt descending, sold descending, t ascending, person ascending, a sample is dropped when it overlaps a sample already kept from a different person by more than half of the shorter interval (overlap = min(t1, t2) - max(t1 - dt1, t2 - dt2)); (3) each kept sample goes to the cell of Spanish local time of mid = t - floor(dt / 2), with or without a price reference. Each cell gains six columns: soldUnits, soldSeconds, soldN (kept samples), soldDays (distinct Spanish local dates of mid, numbered like dayIndex: dayIndex(mid) in winter, dayIndex(mid + 3600) in summer, so the weekday cells of a block never share a day), maxUnits and maxSeconds (the sample with the largest sold, ties: the larger dt; 0, 0 when soldN = 0). A cell can therefore have n = 0 and only sales; an item with only samples is listed with n = 0 and wd = []. Cells: [cell, n, days, sumBp, nQty, sumQtyBp, soldUnits, soldSeconds, soldN, soldDays, maxUnits, maxSeconds]. Implementations must not compare every pair of samples (bucket kept samples per hour of t).",
